// PER-147: two deep presses replayed from Nikita's headset blade log (blade-20261023-174724.csv, "Mirror me" at 100 ms:
// the partner is this Fencer's own hand mirrored and delayed), frame by frame as the app stepped them: both hands'
// blades (guard and real point) through one BladeContactSolver with a Fencer's grip on both, as PartnerBladeContact
// does. On the headset the first (a slow hand, about 0.4 m/s) pressed the blades 50 cm into each other with the
// partner's blade turned 100 to 170 degrees, and the second (a fast sweep, about 2 m/s) a metre, there and back, with
// this Fencer's blade turned up to 171 degrees and shaking. Replayed, no blade turns past the release's 90 degrees, no
// drawn point jumps beyond its hand, nothing shakes, and the pair is let go before the hands press past the through
// depth. Strip frame (+x the Fencer's right, +y up, +z toward the partner), meters, seconds, degrees.
